<!-- begin paragraph -->
<TR>
<TD WIDTH=15% VALIGN=top>
<!-- Add marginal notes below -->
<I>
Plots for Lognormal Distribution
</I>
</TD>
<TD WIDTH=85%>
<!-- Add main text below -->
The following plots were generated for a
<a href="../section3/eda3669.htm">lognormal distribution</a>.
<p>
<IMG SRC="fuller/gif/lognppcc.gif"
     alt="plots generated for a lognormal distribution">

</TD>
</TR>
<!-- end paragraph -->

<!-- begin paragraph -->
<TR>
<TD WIDTH=15% VALIGN=top>
<!-- Add marginal notes below -->
<I>
Conclusions
</I>
</TD>
<TD WIDTH=85%>
<!-- Add main text below -->
We can make the following conclusions from these plots.
<ol>
   <li>The optimal value, in the sense of having the most linear
       probability plot, of the shape parameter
       <img src="../section3/eqns/sigma.gif" alt="sigma"> is 0.18.
       <p>
   <li>At the optimal value of the shape parameter, the PPCC
       value is 0.986.
       <p>
   <li>At the optimal value of the shape parameter, the estimate
       of the location parameter is -9.96 and the estimate of the
       scale parameter is 40.17.
       <p>
   <li>Fine tuning the estimate of the shape parameter (from 0.2 to
       0.18) has minimal impact on the PPCC value.
</ol>

</TD>
</TR>
<!-- end paragraph -->








